## 3. Solution Strategy

The strategic dashboard was developed using metrics that reflect the 3 primary views of the company's business model:

1.  Customer Retention;
2. Customer Segmentation;
3.  Product and Regional Performance.


Each view is represented by the following set of metrics:


1.  Customer Retention View


      - Months with the highest retention in 2014 and 2015;
      - Highest monthly average retention in 2014 and 2015;
      - Lowest monthly average retention in 2014 and 2015;
      - Annual average retention.
     
2.  Customer Segmentation View

      - Percentage of customers per segment;
      - Segment with the highest revenue;
      - Segment requiring attention;
      - Least profitable segments.
      
3.  Product and Regional Performance View

      - Top 10" most and least sold products;
      - Relative percentage of these products compared to the rest;
      - Region that sells the most and the least;
      - Region with the highest and lowest revenue.


## 4. Top 4 Data Insights


1. September 2014 and June 2015 showed the highest average retention. The global average retention for 2014 and 2015 was 10%;
2. The Loyal customer segment accounts for 27% of consumers and drives 51.77% of total customer revenue;
3.  The top 10 most sold products account for 17.53% of total revenue;
4. The East and South regions generate proportionally less revenue (25.85% and 13.47%) relative to their number of orders (27.97% and 16.41%), deviating from the patterns seen in other regions.


